IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fca-nouns`
IMPORT `fca-definitions`

-- Tests for the defined terms of the Frustrated Contracts Act 1959 and for the Interpretation Act words it uses.
-- Expected values are written beside each assertion, from the text of the Act (and, for the Interpretation Act entries, from the
-- Act's words as the copied module prints them), before the run.

§ `Tests -- the terms this Act defines`

-- text, s 2(2): "(referred to in this Act as the time of discharge)"
#ASSERT (`s 2(2) and s 2(4)(a) the term this Act defines` "the time of discharge") EQUALS JUST `s 2(2) definition of the time of discharge`
-- text, s 2(4)(a): "the benefited party", the party obtaining the benefit
#ASSERT (`s 2(2) and s 2(4)(a) the term this Act defines` "the benefited party") EQUALS JUST `s 2(4)(a) label for the benefited party`
-- not covered: any other word is not defined by this Act
#ASSERT (`s 2(2) and s 2(4)(a) the term this Act defines` "frustrated") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 2(2) and s 2(4)(a) the term this Act defines` "valuable benefit") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT sum (map (GIVEN t YIELD 1) `all the terms this Act defines`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 2(2) definition of the time of discharge`'s `what the Act makes it mean` EQUALS "the time when the parties were so discharged, that is, discharged from the further performance of the contract for the reason given in section 2(1)"

§ `Tests -- the Interpretation Act words`

-- Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1), as the copied module prints it: "court" means any court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore.
#ASSERT `what the Act names in defining` "court" EQUALS LIST "any court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore"
#ASSERT `the kind of definition of` "court" EQUALS JUST Means
-- "Government" means the Government of Singapore.
#ASSERT `what the Act names in defining` "Government" EQUALS LIST "Government of Singapore"
-- "person" and "party" include any company or association or body of persons, corporate or unincorporate.
#ASSERT `the kind of definition of` "party" EQUALS JUST Includes
#ASSERT `the kind of definition of` "person" EQUALS JUST Includes
#ASSERT elem "any company" (`what the Act names in defining` "party") EQUALS TRUE
-- the look-up for the words this Act uses: found for the four, NOTHING for any other word, even one the Interpretation Act defines ("month").
#ASSERT `the kind of definition of` "month" EQUALS JUST Means
#ASSERT `Interpretation Act s 2(1) the definition of a word this Act uses` "month" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Interpretation Act s 2(1) the definition of a word this Act uses` "frustrated" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Interpretation Act s 2(1) the definition of a word this Act uses` "court" EQUALS `the definition of` "court"
#ASSERT `Interpretation Act s 2(1) the definition of a word this Act uses` "Government" EQUALS `the definition of` "Government"
#ASSERT `Interpretation Act s 2(1) the definition of a word this Act uses` "party" EQUALS `the definition of` "party"
#ASSERT `Interpretation Act s 2(1) the definition of a word this Act uses` "person" EQUALS `the definition of` "person"
#ASSERT sum (map (GIVEN w YIELD 1) `the words of this Act that the Interpretation Act defines`) EQUALS 4

-- assertions written: 20; satisfied: 20 (check.sh prints the count)
